Subject: [PATCH 30/34] [3.1.1] [M157] Make escaping popups' initial origin
 opaque in the browser too

Original change's description:
> Make escaping popups' initial origin opaque in the browser too
>
> Problem: a popup opened from a CSP-sandboxed document with
> allow-popups-to-escape-sandbox has a non-sandboxed browsing context,
> but its initial empty document still inherits the opener's CSP
> sandbox (crrev.com/c/3643878). So the browser and the renderer
> disagree on the initial empty document's origin.
>
> Currently:
> - The renderer gives the initial empty document an opaque origin,
>   because the document is sandboxed.
> - The browser gives it the opener's origin, because
>   SetOriginDependentStateOfNewFrame() only checks the browsing
>   context's sandbox flags.
> - To make the renderer side work, CreateNewWindow() always sends a
>   sandbox origin token, generating a fallback one when the browser
>   didn't generate one.
>
> This CL:
> - Makes SetOriginDependentStateOfNewFrame() check the initial empty
>   document's sandbox flags instead. These are the browsing context's
>   sandbox flags plus the CSP sandbox inherited from the creator, which
>   is what the renderer uses. So the browser now also gives these
>   popups an opaque origin, derived from the same sandbox origin token
>   as the renderer's, so they match exactly.
> - Removes the fallback token: a token is only sent when the popup's
>   initial empty document is sandboxed.
>
> As a result, for these popups, the browser-side origin, IsolationInfo
> and StorageKey of the initial empty document are now opaque. Nothing
> changes in other cases, where the browsing context's sandbox flags
> already include the creator document's sandbox flags.
>
